From 734623df6b09a59b3079a56533da1bc8c4df1394 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: z060142 <z060142@yahoo.com.tw>
Date: Sun, 23 Aug 2026 22:08:16 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 15/24] feat: lens character (vignette + distortion) and
 documentation pass

Lens character pair, each coupling an explicit tunable property so the
future lens-preset layer can dial in any glass:
- Vignette Amount (0-2) drives the engine's stock vignette map through a
  new strength constant; Vignette Aperture Link (0-1) optionally fades
  it mechanically (strongest wide open, gone by f/5.6). Archaeology: the
  legacy SAMPLE2 gate was inverted, so the stock map never rendered.
- Distortion (-1..+1, + barrel / - pincushion aka wide-angle correction)
  as a corner-safe radial UV remap in the PostAA composite: barrel
  anchors the corners, pincushion anchors the inscribed circle so
  neither direction clamps into edge smears. Distortion Focal Link adds
  the optional zoom characteristic (barrel short / pincushion long,
  pivot 35mm). Overscan render-and-crop recorded as the quality plan-B.
- Both live behind r_HDRVignetteAmount / r_LensDistortion cvars for
  console audition; the component drives them on property change and
  every frame, editor included, with full save/restore.

Documentation pass (agent-written from source, 3 files): both plugin
READMEs rewritten with complete grouped property tables and formulas,
new docs/ConsoleReference.md for all cvars. Doc-driven accuracy fixes:
Exposure Mode default is now actually AutoBiased (member init had
silently overridden the enum default to Manual), ISO/Shutter
descriptions no longer claim "Manual mode only", stale cvar help texts
and comments corrected.

